# A runtime-owned class's field-wise constructor is written only where written
# C builds one by its fields (io_file_by_fields does). This program reaches
# io.File through the standard output stream, which the runtime builds, so the
# File struct is written and its constructor is not.
main: function is {
    b: Bytes
    b.append from: 111.u8
    b.append from: 107.u8
    b.append from: 10.u8
    w: io.stdout
    wr: w.write from: b.byteView
    print "done"
}
